   "date": "2016-01-13T10:21:30Z",
   "subject": "Estimating variance of a dsm analysis with a dummy ddf object",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dear users of Distance,<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am hoping that someone could kindly help me with a problem\r\nthat I have. I’ve being doing a dsm analysis in R involving surveys of rabbit\r\nlatrines. <u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">My problem involves trying to estimate variance when a dummy\r\nddf object is being used.<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The detection function was created in program Distance (why\r\nDistance and not R is a problem best addressed later) and I created a dummy ddf\r\nobject, using the method suggested in the “Dummymrdsobjects” wiki page. The\r\nobservation file looks like:<u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-CreL9Kufl2I/VpYiroklp0I/AAAAAAAAENM/QjtGgsu1Vnw/s1600/obs.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-CreL9Kufl2I/VpYiroklp0I/AAAAAAAAENM/QjtGgsu1Vnw/s1600/obs.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680246000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0F7rMm18xIdjxEgWb8RV1S\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-CreL9Kufl2I/VpYiroklp0I/AAAAAAAAENM/QjtGgsu1Vnw/s320/obs.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"107\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The column “pdf” is the probability that is associated with\r\nthe distance of each sighting. The segment data looks like:</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-gj2qeFgMJus/VpYi4wotyEI/AAAAAAAAENU/Vd9YlnIuiks/s1600/seg.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-gj2qeFgMJus/VpYi4wotyEI/AAAAAAAAENU/Vd9YlnIuiks/s1600/seg.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680246000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3vs9QroyFHCW17ZlKobAs_\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-gj2qeFgMJus/VpYi4wotyEI/AAAAAAAAENU/Vd9YlnIuiks/s320/seg.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"67\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The prediction grid looks like:<u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-h2LGUqXWe5w/VpYjC3kqUsI/AAAAAAAAENc/qT7wYxdNhNo/s1600/pred.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-h2LGUqXWe5w/VpYjC3kqUsI/AAAAAAAAENc/qT7wYxdNhNo/s1600/pred.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680246000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0UIrJSyWpTNqm4B2ZLCTQI\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-h2LGUqXWe5w/VpYjC3kqUsI/AAAAAAAAENc/qT7wYxdNhNo/s320/pred.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"61\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The commands for the ddf dummy were:<u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-SI5VsPrIN-0/VpYjL3FMp7I/AAAAAAAAENk/sNKd9GeJXMI/s1600/ddf.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-SI5VsPrIN-0/VpYjL3FMp7I/AAAAAAAAENk/sNKd9GeJXMI/s1600/ddf.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680246000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3MuOQG2cVsdiJo6LUuguZw\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-SI5VsPrIN-0/VpYjL3FMp7I/AAAAAAAAENk/sNKd9GeJXMI/s320/ddf.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"113\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I then ran a dsm model:<u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-UtEL3e7xXIA/VpYjbEqiAhI/AAAAAAAAENs/Bt0zJxmYFOg/s1600/model%2Bcommand.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-UtEL3e7xXIA/VpYjbEqiAhI/AAAAAAAAENs/Bt0zJxmYFOg/s1600/model%252Bcommand.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680246000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3OTSkUCLKUFwgTlX0XiTgR\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-UtEL3e7xXIA/VpYjbEqiAhI/AAAAAAAAENs/Bt0zJxmYFOg/s1600/model%2Bcommand.jpg\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">and the model printout:<u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-3Q-uF_bziDU/VpYkG0JjnEI/AAAAAAAAEOE/jE4WuaIB-GI/s1600/model%2Bprintout.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-3Q-uF_bziDU/VpYkG0JjnEI/AAAAAAAAEOE/jE4WuaIB-GI/s1600/model%252Bprintout.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680246000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3TBejO0-IDrlm4QPRA006D\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-3Q-uF_bziDU/VpYkG0JjnEI/AAAAAAAAEOE/jE4WuaIB-GI/s320/model%2Bprintout.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"219\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Because\r\nthere is no detection function in the analysis, I tried to run the dsm.var.gam\r\nfunction to estimate variance. However, when I did, I got this error message:</span><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ExnIsM3D4rQ/VpYkUSvAfhI/AAAAAAAAEOM/xAFxJdTBJ-o/s1600/variance%2Bprintout.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ExnIsM3D4rQ/VpYkUSvAfhI/AAAAAAAAEOM/xAFxJdTBJ-o/s1600/variance%252Bprintout.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680246000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08r5P66O0Osks--fIZA1M0\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ExnIsM3D4rQ/VpYkUSvAfhI/AAAAAAAAEOM/xAFxJdTBJ-o/s320/variance%2Bprintout.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"42\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Does anyone know how I should go about estimating variance\r\nfor a dsm analysis that uses a dummy ddf?<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thank you for your time,<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Greg Lollback.<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
