  {
   "id": "sjR9kvyNAgAJ",
   "from": "Greg Lollback",
   "author": "5e8948704a66a501",
   "date": "2016-01-18T23:53:03Z",
   "subject": "Re: Estimating variance of a dsm analysis with a dummy ddf object",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi people,<div><br></div><div>This issue has been sorted. In the end I used a detection function created in the R package Distance and ditched the dummy ddf. This is because of the problem of estimating dsm uncertainty with a dummy ddf. The dummy ddf I was using did not have detection function uncertainty associated with it that &quot;dsm.var.gam&quot; was looking for. Note that when using the argument &quot;ddf.obj=NULL&quot;, the &quot;dsm.var.gam&quot; function won&#39;t try to estimate detection function uncertainty.</div><div><br></div><div>For the sake of someone else having the same issue as me, I once received this error when I tried to predict a dsm model:</div><div><br></div><div>&quot;<i style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">Error in if (score &gt; best$score &amp;&amp; (!only.loose || (lmin &lt;= dmin &amp;&amp; lmax &gt;=  : </i><i style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed&quot;</i></div><div><i style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><br></i></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">This error was caused when the predicted abundance for each grid cell was too high (awful model!) and R replaced the predicted value with &quot;Inf&quot;. &quot;Inf&quot; is short for Infinity!</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">Thank you kindly to David Miller for helping me out of this bother!</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">Greg Lollback<br></span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Wednesday, 13 January 2016 21:21:30 UTC+11, Greg Lollback  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dear users of Distance,</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am hoping that someone could kindly help me with a problem\r\nthat I have. I’ve being doing a dsm analysis in R involving surveys of rabbit\r\nlatrines. </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">My problem involves trying to estimate variance when a dummy\r\nddf object is being used.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The detection function was created in program Distance (why\r\nDistance and not R is a problem best addressed later) and I created a dummy ddf\r\nobject, using the method suggested in the “Dummymrdsobjects” wiki page. The\r\nobservation file looks like:</p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-CreL9Kufl2I/VpYiroklp0I/AAAAAAAAENM/QjtGgsu1Vnw/s1600/obs.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-CreL9Kufl2I/VpYiroklp0I/AAAAAAAAENM/QjtGgsu1Vnw/s1600/obs.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680251000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2oM4mhGaPYZZATmnNaRvI0\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-CreL9Kufl2I/VpYiroklp0I/AAAAAAAAENM/QjtGgsu1Vnw/s320/obs.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"107\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The column “pdf” is the probability that is associated with\r\nthe distance of each sighting. The segment data looks like:</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-gj2qeFgMJus/VpYi4wotyEI/AAAAAAAAENU/Vd9YlnIuiks/s1600/seg.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-gj2qeFgMJus/VpYi4wotyEI/AAAAAAAAENU/Vd9YlnIuiks/s1600/seg.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680251000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2zTOeGQIdXKsw5fapiaTMd\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-gj2qeFgMJus/VpYi4wotyEI/AAAAAAAAENU/Vd9YlnIuiks/s320/seg.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"67\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The prediction grid looks like:</p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-h2LGUqXWe5w/VpYjC3kqUsI/AAAAAAAAENc/qT7wYxdNhNo/s1600/pred.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-h2LGUqXWe5w/VpYjC3kqUsI/AAAAAAAAENc/qT7wYxdNhNo/s1600/pred.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680251000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2NvuZqfMRJgd92a-SKxKsP\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-h2LGUqXWe5w/VpYjC3kqUsI/AAAAAAAAENc/qT7wYxdNhNo/s320/pred.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"61\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The commands for the ddf dummy were:</p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-SI5VsPrIN-0/VpYjL3FMp7I/AAAAAAAAENk/sNKd9GeJXMI/s1600/ddf.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-SI5VsPrIN-0/VpYjL3FMp7I/AAAAAAAAENk/sNKd9GeJXMI/s1600/ddf.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680251000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2LAt71XpD24rWxcHHEekBE\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-SI5VsPrIN-0/VpYjL3FMp7I/AAAAAAAAENk/sNKd9GeJXMI/s320/ddf.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"113\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I then ran a dsm model:</p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-UtEL3e7xXIA/VpYjbEqiAhI/AAAAAAAAENs/Bt0zJxmYFOg/s1600/model%2Bcommand.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-UtEL3e7xXIA/VpYjbEqiAhI/AAAAAAAAENs/Bt0zJxmYFOg/s1600/model%252Bcommand.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680251000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1CHR354gZQB7borAvz24xq\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-UtEL3e7xXIA/VpYjbEqiAhI/AAAAAAAAENs/Bt0zJxmYFOg/s1600/model%2Bcommand.jpg\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">and the model printout:</p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-3Q-uF_bziDU/VpYkG0JjnEI/AAAAAAAAEOE/jE4WuaIB-GI/s1600/model%2Bprintout.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-3Q-uF_bziDU/VpYkG0JjnEI/AAAAAAAAEOE/jE4WuaIB-GI/s1600/model%252Bprintout.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680251000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3k9f0IiRNuvrbfMhLDkehV\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-3Q-uF_bziDU/VpYkG0JjnEI/AAAAAAAAEOE/jE4WuaIB-GI/s320/model%2Bprintout.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"219\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Because\r\nthere is no detection function in the analysis, I tried to run the dsm.var.gam\r\nfunction to estimate variance. However, when I did, I got this error message:</span><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ExnIsM3D4rQ/VpYkUSvAfhI/AAAAAAAAEOM/xAFxJdTBJ-o/s1600/variance%2Bprintout.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ExnIsM3D4rQ/VpYkUSvAfhI/AAAAAAAAEOM/xAFxJdTBJ-o/s1600/variance%252Bprintout.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475680251000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1fWcetelY6AOlVXFMbgSmb\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ExnIsM3D4rQ/VpYkUSvAfhI/AAAAAAAAEOM/xAFxJdTBJ-o/s320/variance%2Bprintout.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"42\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Does anyone know how I should go about estimating variance\r\nfor a dsm analysis that uses a dummy ddf?</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thank you for your time,</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Greg Lollback.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p></div></blockquote></div></div>"
